labelled: 2026-09-24
--- code
export async function getSchemeClaim(requirement: SchemeRequirement, formatName: string): Promise<LedgerClaim> {
  if (window.LegacyLedgerKeys && requirement.scheme === PostingScheme.DirectCash) {
    return getClaimThroughPrefixedSchemeApi(requirement.scheme, window.LegacyLedgerKeys);
  }

  if (typeof ledgerApi.requestSchemeAccess === 'function') {
    return getClaimThroughStandardApi(requirement, formatName);
  }

  return LedgerClaim.Unknown;
}
--- facts
`LegacyLedgerKeys` is the vendor's prefixed scheme interface.
The vendor's ledgers answer DirectCash as unsupported through the standard API, so this branch asks `LegacyLedgerKeys` first.

# claimed at this site by an earlier run:
`window.LegacyLedgerKeys` is the vendor's prefixed interface, and it knows DirectCash alone. Such a ledger reports DirectCash as unsupported through the standard scheme API.

# claimed at this site by an earlier run:
A ledger exposing the vendor's prefixed API answers about DirectCash only there, so a DirectCash question goes to it first. Only DirectCash goes there, because the prefixed API knows the vendor's scheme alone and would answer `Unsupported` about EscrowCredit.
